/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  liquidDensity05_CO2water -- D4 of the liquid-density pilot (C378): a test
  of SELECTION AND REFUSAL, not of accuracy.  x_CO2 0.02 in water at
  293.15 K and 20 MPa; CO2 is a declared Henry solute (diluteSolution).  Its
  volume in the liquid is a partial molar volume (`v_inf`), which this pilot
  does not read, so no pure-liquid volume stands for it and the kernel
  REFUSES -- the SAME refusal at 293.15 K and at 313.15 K, with no switch at
  CO2's critical temperature (304.13 K).  Remedy named: a `v_inf` (a later
  slice) or the declared hypothesis massWithoutVolume; with that hypothesis
  bounded at maxMassFraction 0.01 the run is refused again by its bound
  (w_CO2 0.0475).  Measured, the dissolved CO2 RAISES the density by
  1.55-1.71 % at 293 K (Hebach et al. 2004); a mass-without-volume reading
  could not show that either.  The case is marked `.expect-nonconvergence`:
  its refusal is the lesson, asserted word for word by check_density_pilot.

  The flowsheet of every liquid-density demonstration: feed (1 kg/s) ->
  pump P1 (dP 2 bar, eta 0.7) -> CSTR R1 (V_R 1 m3, the reaction's reactant
  absent, see constant/reactions) -> product.  By hand, with rho the
  property kernel's liquid density printed in the run's table:
      Q   = m_dot / rho                 (the pump's volumetric flow)
      W   = Q dP / eta                  (its shaft power)
      h   = dP / (rho g)                (its head)
      tau = V_R rho / m_dot             (the CSTR's residence time, at its
                                         feed, the pump's outlet state)
  The pump prices its INLET state, the CSTR its FEED (the pump's outlet).
  Theory Guide: sec:liquid-density-methods.  Gate: check_density_pilot.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

units
(
    {
        name        P1;
        type        pump;
        in          feed;
        outputs     ( pumped );
        operation   { dP 2 bar; eta 0.7; }
    }
    {
        name        R1;
        type        cstr;
        in          pumped;
        outputs     ( product );
        operation   { V_R 1; }
        reactions   ( absentAcid );
    }
);
